Third-party fonts

The interface is drawn with fonts bundled by the egui library
(https://github.com/emilk/egui), each under its own license:

- Ubuntu Light: Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0.
- Noto Emoji: SIL Open Font License 1.1.
- Hack: MIT License, with Bitstream Vera License terms for parts of the design.
- emoji-icon-font: MIT License.

These licenses cover the fonts only. The full license texts are distributed
with egui and must accompany any distribution of Pixolotl that includes the
fonts.

The default font for new text is Inter 4.1 (https://github.com/rsms/inter),
Copyright (c) 2016 The Inter Project Authors, bundled in the application in
four styles (Regular, Italic, Bold, Bold Italic) under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1. Its full license text is crates/app/assets/fonts/Inter-LICENSE.txt
and must accompany any distribution of Pixolotl that includes the font.

Third-party color profile

The default profile of new CMYK documents is CGATS21 CRPC6
(CGATS21_CRPC6.icc, 3,462,316 bytes, SHA-256
4ea462ebcc80e2376ebf4a72bd118d1ba92c638edcd718e3c051c3a185586063), bundled
unmodified as published by the ICC profile registry
(https://registry.color.org/profile-registry/profiles/CGATS21_CRPC6.icc) and
kept in the source at crates/color/profiles/CGATS21_CRPC6.icc. It is not
covered by the Apache License. Its copyright notice, as the profile itself
states it:

  Copyright X-Rite, Inc. This profile is made available by IDEAlliance,
  with permission of X-Rite, Inc., and may be used, embedded, exchanged,
  included in commercial software and shared without restriction.  It may
  not be altered without written permission of IDEAlliance except for
  single site use.

The ICC profile registry states that the profile "may be used, embedded,
exchanged, and shared without restriction" and "may not be altered, or sold
without written permission of IDEAlliance". Documents that use it embed it
unaltered.

